_url":"https://github.com/Braxtogoo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Braxtogoo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T04:25:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T04:25:44Z","body":"> I would like to ask if I can have this issue assigned. It seems easy enough for me to make my first-ever contribution if you don't mind. Also, can you give some tips on how to test the bug so I can more easily understand it and fix it?\n\nHowdy @DuartePonce and thanks for taking an interest in this. Sadly I'm not sure how much guidance I can provide as the issue mostly seems to be with documentation, unless the parameter is truly meant to be optional, which I don't have enough experience with the engine side of the code to diagnose, maybe a team member would. All I can really say is that the \"bug\" is very easy to trigger. All you have to do is attempt to call the function without parameters, it will immediately highlight red in the built in script editor and error when running. According to the [migration guide](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.4/tutorials/migrating/upgrading_to_godot_4.4.html) this shouldn't happen as it states the parameter is optional, thus no change should be needed going from 4.3 to 4.4 which is what I'm doing.\n\nIn short, I don't know if the parameter should be optional, or if the migration guide is wrong, which if it is, additional guidance to maintain consistent functionality between 4.3 and 4.4 would be appreciated. If you check my attached MRP it has the \"bug\" ready to view. :)\n\nThanks again!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2699777453/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]